{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CBjNaaZ6WBZTs54No2f4gX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils stress-tests a spec-driven code generation pipeline using GNU utilities as subjects. Specs are derived from C source, Go code is generated by an AI orchestrator, and correctness is verified via differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Human writes PRDs/use cases → orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` → differential tests in `pkg/testutils/` verify parity against GNU binaries. Shared libraries: `pkg/sys/` (syscalls), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (test harness).\n\n**Current state:** Releases 00.0 through 05.3 have specs complete with code at generation tags. Release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) has `spec_complete` status, code not started.\n\n**Current release:** 05.4 — all four use cases (md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) need implementation.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 05.4 is the earliest incomplete release. All four checksum utilities share identical structure (read input → compute hash → print GNU-format output). The only variation is the hash algorithm. These can be implemented together within the 250-line budget (~50 lines each × 4 = ~200 lines production code). Per P2, this task covers implementation only; tests would follow in a subsequent task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum (rel05.4 checksum quartet)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd020-md5sum.yaml (md5sum requirements)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd021-sha1sum.yaml (sha1sum requirements)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd022-sha256sum.yaml (sha256sum requirements)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd023-sha512sum.yaml (sha512sum requirements)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml (md5sum use case)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml (sha1sum use case)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml (sha256sum use case)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml (sha512sum use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml (test suite for differential test cases)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols: differential testing, SIGPIPE handling, graceful skip)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests for test file)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference for cmd/ implementation pattern -- flag parsing, stdin fallback, exit codes)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference for differential test file pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: md5sum implementation using crypto/md5\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha1sum implementation using crypto/sha1\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha256sum implementation using crypto/sha256\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha512sum implementation using crypto/sha512\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests for md5sum against gmd5sum\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests for sha1sum against gsha1sum\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests for sha256sum against gsha256sum\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests for sha512sum against gsha512sum\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement the core hash-and-print loop for all four utilities. Each reads\n          file arguments (or stdin when no arguments or \"-\" is given), computes\n          the hash using the corresponding crypto/* package, and prints one line\n          per input in GNU format: \"<hex-hash>  <filename>\\n\" (two spaces before\n          filename, \"-\" for stdin). Reference the PRD requirements for each utility.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement --check (-c) mode for all four utilities. In check mode, the\n          utility reads a checksum file (lines in GNU format), recomputes hashes\n          for each listed file, and prints \"<filename>: OK\" or \"<filename>: FAILED\".\n          Print a summary line to stderr: \"N computed checksums did NOT match\".\n          Exit 0 if all match, exit 1 if any mismatch or read failure.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement check-mode modifier flags: --quiet/-q (suppress OK lines),\n          --status (suppress all output, exit code only), --warn/-w (warn about\n          improperly formatted checksum lines), --strict (exit non-zero for\n          improperly formatted lines). --binary/-b and --text/-t flags must be\n          accepted but are no-ops on GNU/Linux and macOS (both modes produce\n          identical output).\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for all four utilities. Each test file follows\n          the project pattern: build the Go binary with testutils.BuildBinary,\n          look up the reference binary (gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum, gsha512sum)\n          with exec.LookPath and t.Skip if not found, define []testutils.DiffTest\n          cases covering hash mode and check mode, and run testutils.RunDiffTests.\n          Do NOT install any packages -- use graceful t.Skip via exec.LookPath.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          All four utilities share the same structure. Each main.go is self-contained\n          with no shared internal package -- the hash algorithm is the only variation.\n          Use crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256, crypto/sha512 respectively.\n          Do not create a shared checksum library; the duplication is minimal and\n          keeps each utility independent per the project architecture.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() per the project\n          shared protocol. Import github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          For --check mode parsing, accept both \"<hash>  <filename>\" (binary, two spaces)\n          and \"<hash> <filename>\" (text, one space + asterisk or space). Match GNU\n          coreutils behavior for line format validation.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Reference binary names use the Homebrew g-prefix convention: gmd5sum,\n          gsha1sum, gsha256sum, gsha512sum. Use exec.LookPath and t.Skip if not\n          found, per the graceful-skip shared protocol.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/md5sum/main.go compiles and produces correct md5 hashes matching gmd5sum output\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"cmd/sha1sum/main.go compiles and produces correct sha1 hashes matching gsha1sum output\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"cmd/sha256sum/main.go compiles and produces correct sha256 hashes matching gsha256sum output\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"cmd/sha512sum/main.go compiles and produces correct sha512 hashes matching gsha512sum output\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"All four utilities support --check mode with --quiet, --status, --warn, --strict flags\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"All four test files pass with go test ./cmd/md5sum/ ./cmd/sha1sum/ ./cmd/sha256sum/ ./cmd/sha512sum/\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"Tests gracefully skip (t.Skip) when reference binaries are not in PATH\"\n      - id: AC8\n        text: \"All four utilities call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at startup\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27599,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27599},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1533578d-810f-47a8-af8b-8e2deb1aadb5","uuid":"f57c84c4-e4a3-4cd1-be17-db2c961609b5"}
